== Genealogy ==

[[File:Ohokuninushi family tree.png|thumb|250px|right|Genealogy of Ōkuninushi (''Kojiki''). Blue indicates male deities, red indicates female deities, and yellow indicates unspecified gender.]]

According to the ''Kojiki,'' Shitateruhime is the daughter of {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大国主神|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 大国主}} and {{ill|Takirihime-no-Mikoto|ja|多紀理毘売命|1=Tagorihime|2=ja|3=タキリビメ|4=fr|5=Takiribime|6=zh|7=多紀理毘賣命|1=Tagorihime|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takirihime-no-Mikoto|13=User:Immanuelle/Tagorihime|qq=|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}, making her the sister of {{ill|Ajisukitakahikone|ja|阿遅鉏高日子根神|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ajisukitakahikone|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to アヂスキタカヒコネ}}. This genealogy is also supported by the ''Sendai Kuji Hongi.''

== Shrines ==

Shitateruhime is enshrined at several locations, including:
* {{ill|Hime Shrine|lt=Hime Shrine|lt=Hime Shrine (Toyama)|ja|比賣神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hime Shrine (Toyama)|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 比売神}} in [[:en:Toyama Prefecture|Toyama Prefecture]], where she is the main deity.
* {{ill|Tamatsuoka Shrine|ja|玉津岡神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tamatsuoka Shrine|qq=}} in [[:en:Kyoto Prefecture|Kyoto Prefecture]], dedicated to her worship.
* {{ill|Himekoso Shrine|ja|比売許曽神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Himekoso Shrine|qq=}} in [[:en:Osaka Prefecture|Osaka Prefecture]].
* [[:en:Izumo-taisha|Izumo Taisha]]’s external shrine, known as ''Ōanamochi-no-Miko Tamae Shrine'' (大穴持御子玉江神社).

